REGENT OF CENTRAL BANGKA

REGENT OF CENTRAL BANGKA

PROVINCE OF BANGKA BELITUNG ISLANDS

COPY

REGIONAL REGULATION OF CENTRAL BANGKA REGENCY

NUMBER 2 OF 2014

CONCERNING

EMPOWERMENT AND PROTECTION OF WOMEN

BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD

REGENT OF CENTRAL BANGKA,

Considering : a. that women and men have equal rights to participate in various fields of life;

b. that women are an asset of the nation who play a very important role in the process of continuation and creation of quality generations so they need to receive protection from violence and discrimination and need to be empowered so that they can actualize their potential optimally;

c. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a and letter b, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning Empowerment and Protection of Women;

In view of : 1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;

2. Law Number 1 of 1974 concerning Marriage (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1974 Number 1);

3. Law Number 13 of 1998 concerning Elderly Welfare (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1998 Number 190);

4. Law Number 39 of 1999 concerning Human Rights (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1999 Number 165, Supplement to State Gazette

Number 3886);

5. Law Number 27 of 2000 concerning Establishment of Bangka Belitung Islands Province (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2000 Number 217, Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 403);

6. Law Number 5 of 2003 concerning Establishment of South Bangka Regency, Central Bangka Regency, West Bangka Regency and East Belitung Regency in Bangka Belitung Islands Province (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2003 Number 25, Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4268);

7. Law Number 13 of 2003 concerning Manpower (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2003 Number 39, Supplement to State Gazette Number 4279);

8. Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2004 Number 95, Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4419);

9. Law Number 32 of 2004 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2004 Number 125, Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4437), as has been amended several times most recently by Law

Number 12 of 2008 concerning Second Amendment to Law Number 32 of 2004 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2008 Number 59, Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4844);

10.Law Number 21 of 2007 concerning Eradication of the Crime of Human Trafficking (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2007 Number 58);

11.Law Number 11 of 2009 concerning Social Welfare (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2009 Number 12); 12.Law Number 19 of 2011 concerning Ratification of the Convention on The Rights of Persons With Disabilities (Convention Concerning the Rights of Persons with Disabilities) (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2011 Number 107, Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5251);

13.Government Regulation Number 79 of 2005 concerning Guidelines for Guidance and Supervision of Regional Government Administration (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2005 Number 165, Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4593);

14.Government Regulation Number 38 of 2007 concerning Division of Governmental Affairs between the Government, Provincial Regional Government, and Regency/Municipal Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2007 Number 82, Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4737);

15.Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment Number 2 of 2008 concerning Guidelines for Implementation of Women's Protection; With Joint Approval of

THE REGIONAL HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES OF CENTRAL BANGKA REGENCY and

THE REGENT OF CENTRAL BANGKA

DECIDES:

To Establish : REGIONAL REGULATION CONCERNING EMPOWERMENT AND PROTECTION OF WOMEN.

text:
Pasal 2

Pemberdayaan dan Perlindungan Perempuan, dilaksanakan berdasarkan asas:

a. penghormatan hak asasi manusia;
b. keadilan dan kesetaraan gender;
c. nondiskriminasi; dan
d. perlindungan korban.

translated_text:
Article 2

Empowerment and Protection of Women shall be implemented based on the principles of:

a. respect for human rights;
b. justice and gender equality;
c. non-discrimination; and
d. protection of victims.

text:
Pasal 3

Penyelenggaraan Pemberdayaan dan Perlindungan Perempuan dilaksanakan bertujuan untuk:

a. meningkatkan peran serta perempuan baik secara individual maupun secara kelompok sebagai potensi dan sumber daya dalam penyelenggaraan hidup sosial kemasyarakatan;
b. mencegah segala bentuk diskriminasi;
c. memberdayakan perempuan baik secara individual maupun kelompok dan masyarakat yang mengalami masalah gender agar mampu memenuhi kebutuhannnya secara mandiri;
d. mencegah dan menangani resiko dari kerentanan perempuan agar kelangsungan hidupnya dapat dipenuhi sesuai dengan kebutuhan dasar minimal;
e. menurunnya kesenjangan kesempatan antara perempuan dan laki-laki dalam pencapaian pembangunan; dan
f. menurunnya tindak kekerasan terhadap perempuan.

translated_text:
Article 3

Implementation of Empowerment and Protection of Women is carried out with the aim to:

a. increase the participation of women both individually and in groups as potential and resources in the administration of social community life;
b. prevent all forms of discrimination;
c. empower women both individually and in groups and communities experiencing gender issues to be able to meet their needs independently;
d. prevent and address risks from women's vulnerability so that their survival can be met in accordance with minimum basic needs;
e. reduce the gap in opportunities between women and men in achieving development; and
f. reduce violence against women.

text:
BAB III

HAK ASASI MANUSIA DAN KEBEBASAN DASAR MANUSIA Pasal 4 Hak Asasi Manusia dan kebebasan dasar manusia, terdiri dari:

a. Hak untuk hidup;
b. Hak berkeluarga dan melanjutkan keturunan;
c. Hak mengembangkan diri;
d. Hak memperoleh keadilan;
e. Hak atas kebebasan pribadi;
f. Hak atas rasa aman;
g. Hak atas kesejahteraan; dan h.Hak turut serta dalam pemerintahan.

translated_text:
CHAPTER III

HUMAN RIGHTS AND FUNDAMENTAL FREEDOMS Article 4 Human Rights and fundamental freedoms consist of:

a. Right to life;
b. Right to establish a family and procreate;
c. Right to self-development;
d. Right to obtain justice;
e. Right to personal freedom;
f. Right to security;
g. Right to welfare; and h.Right to participate in government.

text:
Pasal 5

(1) Setiap perempuan berhak untuk:

a. hidup tentram, aman, damai, bahagia, sejahtera lahir dan batin;
b. hidup berkeluarga dalam ikatan perkawinan yang sah;
c. mempertahankan hidup dan meningkatkan taraf hidupnya;
d. memiliki pekerjaan yang disukainya dan berhak pula atas syarat-syarat ketenagakerjaan yang adil;
e. memperoleh pendidikan dan pengajaran di semua jenis, jenjang dan jalur pendidikan sesuai dengan persyaratan yang ditentukan;
f. lingkungan yang sehat dan bersih;
g. mendapatkan upah kerja yang adil sesuai dengan pekerjaannya yang sebanding dan sepadan dengan martabat kemanusiannya;
h. memilih dan/atau dipilih dalam pemilihan umum, pemilihan kepala daerah, pemilihan kepala desa dan/atau pemilihan jabatan politik lainnya berdasarkan persamaan hak melalui pemungutan suara yang langsung, umum, bebas, rahasia, jujur dan adil menurut peraturan perundang-undangan yang berlaku;
i. mendapatkan perlindungan khusus dalam pelaksanaan pekerjaan atau profesinya terhadap hal-hal yang dapat mengancam keselamatan dan/atau kesehatannya berkenaan dengan fungsi reproduksi wanita; dan
j. hak khusus yang melekat pada diri wanita dikarenakan fungsi reproduksinya dijamin dan dlindungi oleh hukum.
(2) Perempuan yang telah dewasa dan atau telah menikah berhak untuk melakukan perbuatan hukum sendiri kecuali ditentukan lain oleh hukum agamanya.
(3) Perkawinan yang sah hanya dapat berlangsung atas kehendak bebas dari pihak perempuan dan pihak laki-laki sesuai dengan peraturan perundang-undangan.
(4) Seorang istri selama dalam ikatan perkawinan mempunyai hak dan tanggung jawab yang sama dengan suaminya atas semua hal yang berkenaan dengan kehidupan perkawinannya, hubungan dengan anak anaknya dan hak pemilikan serta pengelolaan harta bersama.
(5) Setelah putusan perkawinannya seorang perempuan mempunyai hak dan tanggung jawab yang sama dengan mantan suaminya atas semua hal yang berkenaan dengan anak-anaknya, dengan memperhatikan kepentingan terbaik bagi anak.
(6) Setelah putusan perkawinan, seorang perempuan mempunyai hak yang sama dengan mantan suaminya atas semua hal yang berkenaan dengan harta bersama tanpa mengurangi hak anak, sesuai dengan ketentuan peraturan perundang-undangan.
(7) Setiap perempuan yang dalam kondisi disabilitas, usia lanjut, hamil berhak memperoleh kemudahan dan perlakuan khusus.
(8) Setiap perempuan lanjut usia, disabilitas fisik dan/atau mental, berhak memeroleh perawatan, pendidikan, pelatihan dan bantuan khusus atas biaya pemerintahan daerah untuk menjamin kehidupan yang layak sesuai dengan martabat kemanusiannya.

translated_text:
Article 5

(1) Every woman has the right to:

a. live in tranquility, security, peace, happiness, and prosperity both physically and spiritually;
b. live in a family within the bond of a lawful marriage;
c. sustain life and improve her standard of living;
d. have work that she likes and is also entitled to fair employment conditions;
e. obtain education and instruction in all types, levels and paths of education in accordance with the stipulated requirements;
f. a healthy and clean environment;
g. obtain fair wages in accordance with her work that is comparable and commensurate with her human dignity;
h. vote and/or be elected in general elections, regional head elections, village head elections and/or other political office elections based on equal rights through direct, general, free, secret, honest and fair voting according to the applicable laws and regulations;
i. obtain special protection in the performance of her work or profession against things that may threaten her safety and/or health with regard to women's reproductive function; and
j. special rights inherent to women due to their reproductive function are guaranteed and protected by law.
(2) Women who are adults and/or married have the right to perform legal acts independently unless otherwise determined by their religious law.
(3) A lawful marriage can only take place by the free will of the woman and the man in accordance with laws and regulations.
(4) A wife during the marriage bond has the same rights and responsibilities as her husband in all matters concerning her marital life, relations with her children and the rights of ownership and management of joint property.
(5) After the dissolution of her marriage, a woman has the same rights and responsibilities as her former husband in all matters concerning her children, taking into account the best interests of the child.
(6) After the dissolution of marriage, a woman has the same rights as her former husband in all matters concerning joint property without diminishing the rights of children, in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.
(7) Every woman who is disabled, elderly, pregnant is entitled to facilities and special treatment.
(8) Every elderly woman, with physical and/or mental disabilities, is entitled to receive care, education, training and special assistance at the expense of the regional government to ensure a decent life in accordance with her human dignity.

text:
Pasal 12

Pelaksanaan kebijakan, program dan kegiatan perlindungan perempuan, dapat dilakukan dengan upaya:

a. melakukan kerjasama dengan dunia usaha, lembaga nonpemerintah, perusahaan swasta, Yayasan, dan lembaga di dalam negeri lainnya serta lembaga internasional, sesuai dengan ketentuan peraturan perundang-undangan;
b. melakukan kerjasama daerah, sesuai dengan ketentuan peraturan perundang-undangan yang berlaku;
c. menyediakan dan memfasilitasi pelayanan perlindungan perempuan;
d. menyusun sistem pendataan perlindungan perempuan; dan
e. melaksanakan koordinasi pelaksanaan kebijakan, program dan kegiatan perlindungan perempuan antar Satuan Kerja Perangkat Daerah.

translated_text:
Article 12

The implementation of policies, programs and activities for women's protection may be carried out through efforts to:

a. cooperate with the business world, non-government institutions, private companies, Foundations, and other domestic institutions as well as international institutions, in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations;
b. conduct regional cooperation, in accordance with the provisions of applicable laws and regulations;
c. provide and facilitate women's protection services;
d. compile a women's protection data system; and
e. implement coordination of the implementation of policies, programs and activities for women's protection among Regional Apparatus Work Units.

text:
Pasal 13

(1) Penyediaan dan fasilitasi pelayanan perlindungan perempuan sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 12 huruf c berupa:

a. identifikasi korban;
b. bantuan hukum;
c. rehabilitasi medis;
d. rehabilitasi psikososial;
e. reintegrasi sosial;
f. bantuan pemulangan; atau
g. bentuk lainnya.
(2) Penyediaan dan fasilitasi pelayanan perlindungan perempuan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) diberikan pada perempuan:
a. korban kekerasan;
b. korban perdagangan orang;
c. lanjut usia yang tidak mandiri;
d. disabilitas;
e. korban eksploitasi seksual;
f. kepala keluarga;
g. daerah rawan konflik dan bencana;
h. pekerja; dan
i. kelompok rentan lainnya.

translated_text:
Article 13

(1) Provision and facilitation of women's protection services as referred to in Article 12 letter c shall be in the form of:

a. victim identification;
b. legal assistance;
c. medical rehabilitation;
d. psychosocial rehabilitation;
e. social reintegration;
f. repatriation assistance; or
g. other forms.
(2) Provision and facilitation of women's protection services as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be provided to women who are:
a. victims of violence;
b. victims of human trafficking;
c. elderly who are not independent;
d. disabled;
e. victims of sexual exploitation;
f. heads of households;
g. in conflict and disaster-prone areas;
h. workers; and
i. other vulnerable groups.
